This argument has come up a few times. The big difference is that the 
game mechanics are designed to randomize descriptions. If you bypass 
this randomization, you're bypassing a part of the game, which is 
essentially what cheating is. You could compare it to patching the game 
in a way that changes the actual gameplay; weapons mods and such. If you 
don't want to call it cheating (I'm not saying it necessarily is), 
that's fine. Just acknowledge you're not playing the same game that the 
rest of us are playing.

If I were to try to completely roleplay my PCs, which I never claim to 
do, then you'd be correct and I'd have to be ignorant of the world. But 
then, it wouldn't really be a game anymore.

